-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-left:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1rem 1.35rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">In-migration.</strong><span style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"> Myrtle Beach is the second fastest-growing metro area in the country (U.S. Census Bureau, latest estimates), and North Carolina is the top source of buyers.</span></div>
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-left:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1rem 1.35rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Constrained supply.</strong><span style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"> Coastal land is finite and building has not kept pace with arrivals. More buyers than homes pushes prices up.</span></div>
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-left:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1rem 1.35rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Affordability.</strong><span style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"> Named the 4th most affordable beach town in America by House Beautiful, so out-of-state buyers arriving with home-sale equity stretch further here and keep demand high.</span></div>
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-left:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1rem 1.35rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Unique SC tax breaks.</strong><span style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"> South Carolina does not tax Social Security income, taxes a primary home at a 4% assessment ratio, fully exempts 100% disabled veterans from property tax on their home, and gives owners 65 and older a Homestead exemption on the first $50,000 of value (SC Department of Revenue).</span></div>
