-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Are there first-time buyer programs in the Myrtle Beach area?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. South Carolina housing programs (through SC Housing) and some lender programs offer down-payment assistance and first-time-buyer loans. Eligibility depends on your income, the purchase price, and the location."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How much do I need for a down payment?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Less than most first-timers expect. Down-payment assistance can cover part or all of it, and loan types like FHA and VA lower or eliminate the down payment. The exact cash to close depends on your loan and program, a licensed agent and lender can tell you your real number."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Who counts as a first-time buyer?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "For most South Carolina programs, a first-time buyer is someone who has not owned their primary residence in the last three years. Some programs waive that in certain targeted areas or for veterans."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can a condo be my first home, and can I finance it?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Often yes, condos are one of the most attainable entry points here. The building itself has to be lender-approved, and some oceanfront and condotel buildings are harder to finance. We check a specific building's financeability before you make an offer."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I have to already live in South Carolina to use these programs?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. The home has to be in South Carolina and be your primary residence, but you can qualify while relocating from another state. If you're moving here, our relocation guide walks through the rest."}}]}</script>
