-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">First-Time Buyers &middot; Myrtle Beach, SC</p>
-<h1 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3rem);color:var(--navy);line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:1.1rem;letter-spacing:-.02em">Your first home in Myrtle Beach may take less cash than you think.</h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Chapter3 Realty &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 27, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">What a first-time buyer can afford in Myrtle Beach, the down-payment help South Carolina offers, and the condo and inland-house entry points most first-timers start with.</p>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:700px;margin-bottom:1.8rem">Buying your first home on the Grand Strand is not like buying your first home anywhere else. You are competing with out-of-state cash buyers, working through bylaws and insurance that surprise first-timers. This page covers what matters, and how to find out what you qualify for in one phone call.</p>
