-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">What surprises buyers here?</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">First-time buyer mistakes specific to Myrtle Beach</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A few Grand Strand realities first-time buyers routinely miss:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1.2rem;padding-left:1.2rem;display:grid;gap:.55rem"><li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Flood zones.</strong> Flood insurance can add real monthly cost, so check the zone before you fall for a house.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Wind and hail.</strong> Near the coast this is often a separate policy from your regular homeowners insurance.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Condo costs.</strong> The building's master insurance, HOA fees, and special assessments can change the math overnight.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you write an offer, we pull the HOA bylaws, budget, reserve study, and financials so there are no surprises. Your lender will usually require only hazard insurance, plus flood insurance if the home is in a flood zone.</p>
