-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Down-payment help you may qualify for</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">You may need far less cash than you think</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina runs real first-time-buyer assistance through <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">SC Housing</strong>, the state housing finance authority, and some lenders layer their own help on top. The main forms: Run the actual number with our <a href="/buyers/closing-costs/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">SC closing costs calculator</a>.</p>
-<ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1.2rem;padding-left:1.2rem">
-<li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Down-payment assistance (DPA)</strong>, a second loan that covers some or all of your down payment and closing costs, sometimes forgivable over time.</li>
-<li><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">SC Housing homebuyer loans</strong>, competitive fixed-rate mortgages designed to pair with that assistance.</li>
-</ul>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether you qualify comes down to a few things: your income vs. the county limit, the home's price vs. the program limit, whether you're a first-time buyer, your credit, and a short homebuyer-education course. A first-time buyer generally means you haven't owned your primary home in the last three years. The exact dollar figures and income limits change, so rather than post numbers that go stale, we confirm the current ones with SC Housing and their approved lenders for your specific situation.</p>
-<p style="margin-bottom:0"><a href="/buyers/programs/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">See South Carolina housing programs &rarr;</a> &nbsp; <a href="/buyers/programs/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Lender down-payment assistance &rarr;</a></p>
-</div></section>
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common Questions</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2>
-<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Are there first-time buyer programs in the Myrtle Beach area?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">Yes. South Carolina housing programs (through SC Housing) and some lender programs offer down-payment assistance and first-time-buyer loans. Eligibility depends on your income, the purchase price, and the location.</p></div>
-<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How much do I need for a down payment?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">Less than most first-timers expect. Down-payment assistance can cover part or all of it, and loan types like FHA and VA lower or eliminate the down payment. The exact cash to close depends on your loan and program, a licensed agent and lender can tell you your real number.</p></div>
-<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Who counts as a first-time buyer?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">For most South Carolina programs, a first-time buyer is someone who has not owned their primary residence in the last three years. Some programs waive that in certain targeted areas or for veterans.</p></div>
-<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can a condo be my first home, and can I finance it?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">Often yes, condos are one of the most attainable entry points here. The building itself has to be lender-approved, and some oceanfront and condotel buildings are harder to finance. We check a specific building's financeability before you make an offer.</p></div>
-<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do I have to already live in South Carolina to use these programs?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">No. The home has to be in South Carolina and be your primary residence, but you can qualify while relocating from another state. If you're moving here, our <a href="/buyers/relocating/" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">relocation guide</a> walks through the rest.</p></div>
-<div style="text-align:center;margin-top:2.5rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Find out what you qualify for</a><p style="font-size:.65rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:1.5rem auto 0">Chapter3 Realty is not a lender. South Carolina program information is sourced from the SC State Housing Finance and Development Authority (schousing.sc.gov). Programs, rates, income limits, and availability change without notice. Equal Housing Opportunity.</p></div>
-</div></section>
