pan x="165.8" dy="0">Surfside Beach</tspan></text><circle cx="125.7" cy="227.5" r="5.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><text x="114.7" y="233.5" text-anchor="end" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"><tspan x="114.7" dy="0">Conway</tspan></text><circle cx="187.1" cy="124.1" r="5.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><text x="198.1" y="130.1" text-anchor="start" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"><tspan x="198.1" dy="0">Loris</tspan></text><circle cx="67.6" cy="150.7" r="5.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><text x="67.6" y="137.7" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"><tspan x="67.6" dy="0">Aynor</tspan></text><circle cx="248.8" cy="181.1" r="5.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><text x="237.8" y="182.1" text-anchor="end" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"><tspan x="237.8" dy="0">Longs</tspan></text><circle cx="294.8" cy="210.0" r="5.5" fill="#fff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><text x="304.8" y="226.0" text-anchor="start" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"><tspan x="304.8" dy="0">Little River</tspan></text><circle cx="128.2" cy="354.9" r="5.5" fill="#fff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><text x="138.2" y="372.9" text-anchor="start" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"><tspan x="138.2" dy="0">Murrells Inlet</tspan></text><circle cx="178.1" cy="260.2" r="3.5" fill="none" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><text x="171.1" y="281.2" text-anchor="end" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="18" font-style="italic" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round">Carolina Forest</text><circle cx="140.9" cy="297.3" r="3.5" fill="none" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><text x="131.9" y="306.3" text-anchor="end" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="18" font-style="italic" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round">Socastee</text></g></svg><div class="c3-pg-key" aria-hidden="true"><span><i style="background:rgba(196,120,58,.6);border:1px solid #91592b"></i>Outside USDA's area</span><span><i style="background:#fdfbf7;border:1px solid #5c6b78"></i>Inside USDA's area</span><span><i style="background:#d3e0e5"></i>Atlantic Ocean</span></div></div><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin-top:.6rem">Our map of USDA's home loan area in Horry County. The shaded coast is outside it. Map: Chapter3 Realty, from USDA Rural Development's eligibility map and Census TIGER/Line county lines and coast.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We checked every house for sale at or under $450,000 in Horry County against USDA's map. About six in ten were inside USDA's area.</p><figure style="margin:1.2rem 0 1rem;max-width:560px"><table class="c3-pg-tbl"><caption>Houses for sale at or under $450,000 inside USDA's area on our map</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Town</th><th scope="col">Inside USDA's area</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Aynor</th><td>All</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Loris</th><td>All</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Conway</th><td>Nearly all</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Longs</th><td>About nine in ten</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Little River</th><td>About one in four</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Myrtle Beach</th><td>Fewer than one in ten</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">North Myrtle Beach</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Surfside Beach</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Murrells Inlet</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Murrells Inlet counts only its homes in Horry County.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A home near the edge can fall on either side, so we check each address on USDA's own lookup before you make an offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/va-loans/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">VA loan guide</a> explains who can use a VA loan.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-program"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Which program">Which SC Housing program fits you in Horry County?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Four SC Housing programs are open to Horry County buyers now. A fifth, Palmetto Heroes, is closed until its next round. The voucher program works only where the local housing authority takes part. Find the line that matches you.</p><ul class="c3-pg-pick" role="list" aria-label="Which SC Housing program fits you"><li><span class="c3-pg-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="if">You own no other property, your household is under the income limit, and the home costs $450,000 or less.</span><span class="go">The Homebuyer Program<small>The $10,000 on this page</small></span></span></li><li><span class="c3-pg-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="if">You earn more, the home costs more than $450,000, you already own a home, or you want a manufactured home.</span><span class="go">Palmetto Home Advantage<small>Up to 4 percent of the loan, forgiven after 10 years</small></span></span></li><li><span class="c3-pg-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><span class="if">You are a teacher, nurse, police officer, firefighter, EMT, veteran, or in the military or National Guard.</span><span class="go">Palmetto Heroes<small>$10,000, closed for 2026</small></span></span></li><li><span class="c3-pg-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 20.5v-1a5 5 0 0 1 5-5h2a5 5 0 0 1 5 5v1M16 14.5h1a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="7" r="3.2"/><circle cx="17" cy="8.8" r="2.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="if">You, or anyone in your household, has a permanent disability shown by Social Security disability income (SSI or SSDI) or long-term disability income.</span><span class="go">Families with Disabilities<small>The same 15-year forgivable help, homes up to $450,000</small></span></span></li><li><span class="c3-pg-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><span class="if">You have had a Housing Choice Voucher (Section 8) for at least a year in the county where you buy.</span><span class="go">Voucher homeownership<small>Where the local housing authority takes part</small></span></span></li></ul><h3 id="palmetto-home-advantage" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Palmetto Home Advantage</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Palmetto Home Advantage counts only the borrowers' own income, not the whole household: up to $140,000, for any household size. SC Housing has no price limit for it, but the FHA, VA, USDA or conventional loan still has its own. A repeat buyer may hold at most two financed homes, the new one included. If you sell, refinance or move out within the 10 years, you repay all of the help.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Palmetto Heroes and Families with Disabilities</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Palmetto Heroes' 2026 round filled in about four weeks, after 272 loans. SC Housing has not published a date for the next round. A buyer needs a signed sales contract to get the help, so we start the home search before it opens.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Families with Disabilities is open in every county, has no first-time buyer rule, and uses FHA, VA or USDA loans.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="local-help"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Local help">Is there down payment help from Horry County or Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not from the county or the cities directly. Horry County runs HUD's HOME program for Horry, Georgetown and Williamsburg counties, and that money goes to developers and nonprofits, not to buyers. Two other routes help buyers themselves.</p><ul class="c3-pg-pick" role="list" aria-label="Down payment help from local groups in Horry County"><li><span class="c3-pg-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="go" style="margin:0 0 .35rem"><a href="https://habitathorry.org/what-we-do/homeownership/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Habitat for Humanity of Horry County</a><small>Builds and sells homes</small></span><span class="if">For households earning 35 to 80 percent of the county's median income: for three people in 2026, about $23,000 to $62,000 a year. You must have lived in Horry County for the last 12 months. Buyers put in at least 180 hours of work. You start with a short interest form on its homeownership page, and Habitat pairs you with a volunteer Financial Mentor.</span></span></li><li><span class="c3-pg-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><span class="go" style="margin:0 0 .35rem"><a href="https://corp.fhlbatl.com/who-we-are/news/federal-home-loan-bank-of-atlanta-allocates-120-million-for-affordable-housing-in-2026/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Federal Home Loan Bank of Atlanta</a><small>Grants through member banks</small></span><span class="if"><span style="display:block">Earning under 80 percent of the area's median income: up to $17,500 for a first-time buyer, and up to $20,000 for police, teachers, firefighters, health care workers and veterans.</span> <span style="display:block;margin-top:.45rem">Earning 80 to 120 percent: up to $15,000, from its Workforce Housing Plus+ grants.</span></span></span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The bank grants go through banks that applied for them, and we find out which nearby banks still have money.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you use a bank grant and SC Housing's $10,000 together?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, if the grant's own rules allow it. SC Housing's checklist for the lender has a line for a grant from anyone else, and the lender puts the grant's approval letter in the file.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-to-apply"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="How to apply">How do you apply for SC Housing's down payment help?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You apply through an SC Housing approved lender, in the five steps below. The lender handles the application and the reservation.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is the $10,000 open now?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. SC Housing's program page offers the $10,000. The only program it lists as closed is Palmetto Heroes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The money is limited, and SC Housing pays it out while money lasts. Once the lender reserves your loan and the $10,000, SC Housing holds them for 60 days on an existing home or 120 days on a new one, and the lender can ask for more time.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The five steps</h3><ol class="c3-pg-steps"><li><strong>Pick an SC Housing approved lender.</strong>SC Housing's <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/homebuyers/find-lender?county=166" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find a Lender list for Horry County</a> has about 90 loan officers at about 40 companies. The lender takes your application and checks that you qualify.</li><li><strong>Take the homebuyer course.</strong>The lender arranges it. One buyer finishes it, online or in a classroom, before the loan is approved.</li><li><strong>Find a home under the limit with us.</strong>We search houses, townhomes and condos at or under $450,000 in the towns you pick.</li><li><strong>Reserve the money.</strong>Once you qualify and decide to go ahead, the lender reserves your loan and the $10,000.</li><li><strong>Close.</strong>The $10,000 goes toward your down payment, closing costs and prepaid items at closing. It cannot pay a real estate commission or an appraisal gap, which is the difference when a home appraises for less than its price.</li></ol><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our preferred lender is not on SC Housing's lender list for Horry County, so when one of these programs fits you, we introduce you to an approved lender.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">If you still own a home somewhere else</h3><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> Dana rents in Myrtle Beach and still owns a house in Ohio.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">She wants SC Housing's down payment help for a house in Conway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Her Chapter3 agent finds the problem before she makes an offer. SC Housing will not close the Conway loan while she owns the Ohio house.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">The agent writes the Conway closing date into the contract for a day after the Ohio sale closes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">What this means for you: set the closing on your new home for after the sale of the old one.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/first-time-home-buyer-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">first-time home buyer guide</a> explains the rest of the purchase, step by step. If you are deciding where to look, our guide to the <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">most affordable places to live</a> around Myrtle Beach describes each one.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="sc-housing-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">SC Housing questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I have to be a first-time buyer in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Horry County is one of SC Housing's "targeted" counties, where the first-time buyer rule does not apply. A buyer who has owned a home before can use the $10,000 once that home is sold.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use SC Housing's help on a new home from a builder?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, if the price is $450,000 or less. SC Housing has a form for the builder who sells the home. Its lender list for Horry County includes DHI Mortgage, Lennar Mortgage and NVR Mortgage Finance, the mortgage companies of the builders D.R. Horton, Lennar and NVR.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can the seller pay part of my closing costs with SC Housing's help?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, within the limits of your FHA, VA, USDA or conventional loan. SC Housing's guide adds no limit of its own on help from the seller.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who decides the interest rate on an SC Housing loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">SC Housing decides the rate on its own first mortgage. It is a fixed rate, posted every day for its approved lenders, and your lender locks it for you when it reserves the loan. SC Housing makes the loan with or without the $10,000, so we have the lender quote it both ways before you choose.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I get SC Housing's Made It Home! help or its tax credit in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. SC Housing's Made It Home! help is only for new homes in five other cities, and its Mortgage Credit Certificate, a federal tax credit for buyers, has ended.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/homebuyers/programs-homebuyers" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Housing programs</a>, <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/sites/schousing/files/Documents/Homebuyers/Training-Material/COMBINED%20TRAINING%2003.2026.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Housing program guide</a>, <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/sites/schousing/files/Documents/Homebuyers/2026-2027%20(LENDER)SC%20Housing%20Homebuyer%20Home%20Price%20and%20Income%20Limits%20(06.01.2026).pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026/2027 limits</a>, <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/homebuyers/find-lender?county=166" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Housing Find a Lender</a>, <a href="https://entp.hud.gov/idapp/html/condlook.cfm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD condo list</a>, <a href="https://eligibility.sc.egov.usda.gov/eligibility/welcomeAction.do?pageAction=sfp" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USDA address lookup</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table?q=B19013&g=050XX00US45051" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census income</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table?q=B25118&g=050XX00US45051" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census renter income</a>, <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/homebuyers/programs-homebuyers/housing-choice-voucher-homeownership-program" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Housing voucher homeownership</a>, <a href="https://horrycountysc.gov/departments/community-development/grants/housing/home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County HOME program</a>, <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/news/sc-housings-palmetto-heroes-program-closes-26-registering-272-home-loans" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Housing news</a>. Homes for sale: Chapter3's count of MLS listings, in aggregate, by mailing address and list price; each placed on USDA's map. Not loan or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">A house in Conway's historic district. Photo: Pollinator, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Home_in_the_historic_district,_Conway,_South_Carolina_(18_November_2006).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><div id="afba" style="margin:1.4rem 0 3rem;max-width:640px"><p style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.4rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Affiliated Business Arrangement Disclosure.</strong> Chapter3 Realty Corp has a business relationship with BrickWood Mortgage (NMLS #189497). Because of this relationship, referrals to BrickWood Mortgage may provide Chapter3 Realty a financial or other benefit.</p><p style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7">You are NOT required to use BrickWood Mortgage as a condition for the purchase, sale, or refinance of any property. There are frequently other settlement service providers available with similar services. You are free to shop around to determine that you are receiving the best services and the best rate for those services.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Find a home that fits SC Housing's limits</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Send us your household size and price range. We tell you which program fits, check each condo building's approval and each address on USDA's map, and send the homes that pass.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask which program fits</a></div></section></main>
+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">SC Down Payment Help</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Buying a home</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Down payment help in Horry County:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">you do not have to be a <span style="white-space:nowrap">first-time buyer.</span></em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 4, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">SC Housing gives an eligible buyer $10,000. Most houses for sale in Conway, Loris, Aynor and Longs are under its price limit. Across the beach towns, about a third are.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The $10,000 is a second mortgage from SC Housing, the state's housing agency. A second mortgage is a second loan on the home. It pays toward the down payment and closing costs. After you have lived in the home 15 years, SC Housing forgives it, and you owe nothing on the $10,000. If you sell, refinance or move out sooner, you repay all of it, from the sale or the new loan.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">To qualify, a household of one or two can earn up to $114,960, or $134,120 for three or more. The home can cost up to $450,000, you need a credit score of 640, and you must own no other property when the loan closes.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Homes that fit SC Housing's limits, sent to you</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#qualify" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Do you qualify</a></li><li><a href="#paying-it-back" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Paying it back</a></li><li><a href="#which-homes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which homes</a></li><li><a href="#no-money-down" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">No money down</a></li><li><a href="#which-program" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which program</a></li><li><a href="#local-help" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Local help</a></li><li><a href="#how-to-apply" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How to apply</a