+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Second Home</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Second homes</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Where should you buy a second home near Myrtle Beach?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Six places on the beach, from Cherry Grove to Pawleys Island.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 4, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Six places on the beach, their rental rules and the yearly tax on a second home.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a boat at your back door, buy on the Cherry Grove canals in North Myrtle Beach. For a condo on the sand with the boardwalk outside, buy on the Myrtle Beach oceanfront. For an old beach house on an island with no hotels, buy on Pawleys Island.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach, Pawleys Island and the county outside the cities allow nightly rentals. The City of Myrtle Beach and Surfside Beach allow them only in some zones. Property tax on a $400,000 second home is about $4,800 to $6,100 a year.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="where"><div class="wrap"><style id="c3-glass">main#main{--g-ink:#8a5226;--g-ink-lg:#a8612c;--g-edge:rg