-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">VA Loans</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Military and veterans</p><h1 class="detail-h1">VA loans in Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">which condos and homes qualify.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 2, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Your VA loan can buy most kinds of home here, but a condo must be in one of about 175 Horry County communities on the VA's list.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a house you will live in, yes, if the seller agrees and it passes the VA appraisal. About half the houses for sale on the Grand Strand are marked as taking a VA loan. A condo needs a community on the VA's list, and few oceanfront resort towers are on it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the VA rates you permanently and totally disabled from your service, you pay no property tax on your home. On a home the county values at $400,000, that saves about $1,470 to $2,610 a year.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:v