+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/hoa/">HOA Guide</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Special Assessments</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">HOA Guide</p><h1 class="detail-h1">The buyer of a Myrtle Beach condo can owe the seller's special assessment<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">What one costs, who pays it, and how we find it in the board's minutes.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 4, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">An agent reads a Myrtle Beach condo board's meeting minutes for you, so you know about a coming special assessment before you make an offer.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A special assessment is a one-time bill from a condo association, which all the owners belong to, on top of the regular dues. It pays for a cost the yearly budget and the reserve fund, the money saved for big repairs, do not cover. South Carolina law puts no limit on the amount. Your share is your unit's percentage, set in the condo's founding papers, recorded when the condo was created.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If a seller leaves an assessment unpaid, the association can collect it from the buyer too. The buyer's limit is the amount on the association's written statement of what the seller owes. We get that statement before closing, the day the sale is final.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Know about an assessment before you sign.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us check a building</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#what-it-is" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What it is</a></li><li><a href="#how-much" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How much</a></li><li><a href="#building-age" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Building age</a></li><li><a href="#votes-and-limits" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Votes and limits</a></li><li><a href="#how-we-spot-one" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How to spot one</a></li><li><a href="#who-pays-at-sale" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who pays at sale</a></li><li><a href="#loans" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;tex