 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"When will I-73 be complete in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No date has been announced. SCDOT has not identified the money for most of the estimated 1.6 billion dollar cost, and work cannot begin until it does."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are Horry County impact fees?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A single-family home of about 1,500 square feet pays 1,615 dollars in total under the county's current schedule. A larger home or another type of building pays a different amount."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Was a road tax on the Horry County ballot in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The 2026 Horry County ballot had no ballot question. Voters approved the RIDE IV sales tax in 2024, with 56.78 percent voting yes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who can change impact fees in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The county council, by ordinance with a positive majority, after a report on the effect on affordable housing. The state Development Impact Fee Act allows the fees."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Horry County still building as many homes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The county's 2025 count was 6,418 single-family homes, after 7,269 in 2024, the most of any year from 2005 to 2025."}}]}</script>
