-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Rent prices</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Long-term rents</p><h1 class="detail-h1">How much does a house rent for in Myrtle Beach?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Myrtle Beach rents by bedroom, and what changes them.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated September 7, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The federal rent benchmark for Horry County is $1,504 for two bedrooms and $1,823 for three. A house rents above or below it depending on location, condition and lease length.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Have us run the rent</a></div></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two public numbers describe long-term rents here. The federal fair market rent for Horry County, fiscal year 2027, is $1,258 for one bedroom, $1,504 for two, $1,823 for three and $1,981 for four. Utilities are included. Forty out of 100 standard homes rent at or below it, so most rent for more. The metro's typical asking rent across all home types was about $1,714 in July 2026. One house rents above or below those numbers on bedroom count, location, condition, whether it is furnished, and lease length. Our analyzer estimates the rent for any address, and an agent runs the number from local leases before you offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is the benchmark rent in Horry County?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/fmr2027/FY27_FMRs.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The federal fair market rent</a> is the government's estimate of rent in this metro area. It is published each year for the voucher program and other housing programs. <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">It is the rent that 40 out of 100 standard homes rent at or below</a>. Most standard homes rent for more. The number includes utilities.</p><svg viewBox="0 0 600 134" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Fair market rent by bedroom count, Horry County, fiscal year 2027" style="display:block;max-width:600px;font-family:var(--sans);margin:.6rem 0 1.2rem"><text x="120" y="17" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Studio</text><rect x="128" y="2" width="211" height="20" fill="#c4783a"><title>Studio: $1,155</title></rect><text x="345" y="17" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">$1,155</text><text x="120" y="43" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">One bedroom</text><rect x="128" y="28" width="230" height="20" fill="#c4783a"><title>One bedroom: $1,258</title></rect><text x="364" y="43" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">$1,258</text><text x="120" y="69" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Two bedrooms</text><rect x="128" y="54" width="275" height="20" fill="#c4783a"><title>Two bedrooms: $1,504</title></rect><text x="409" y="69" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">$1,504</text><text x="120" y="95" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Three bedrooms</text><rect x="128" y="80" width="333" height="20" fill="#c4783a"><title>Three bedrooms: $1,823</title></rect><text x="467" y="95" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">$1,823</text><text x="120" y="121" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Four bedrooms</text><rect x="128" y="106" width="362" height="20" fill="#c4783a"><title>Four bedrooms: $1,981</title></rect><text x="496" y="121" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">$1,981</text></svg><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Bedrooms</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Fair market rent, federal fiscal year 2027</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Studio</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,155</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">One</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,258</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,504</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Three</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,823</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,981</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The second public number is a market index. <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The typical asking rent for the Myrtle Beach metro</a> across houses, townhouses and apartments was about $1,714 in July 2026. It was about $1,695 in September 2025. Asking rents are what landlords list, not what tenants sign, and they move with the season here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What changes the rent on one Myrtle Beach house?</h2><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Effect on the rent</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Bedroom count</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The benchmark rises $158 to $319 with each bedroom. Leases here follow the same shape.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Location</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">East of Highway 17 or on the water rents above the same house west of it.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/invest/student-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Near the university</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Rents by the room, on the academic calendar.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Condition and age</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A renovated kitchen and a newer roof rent for more, and rent faster.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Furnished, on a short lease</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">More per month than the same house unfurnished on a twelve-month lease.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A lease matched to a season or a semester</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Rents for more.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="/invest/where-to-buy/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Where to buy a rental, by strategy</a>, with each part of the Grand Strand in one table.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How do you find out what one Myrtle Beach house will rent for?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two ways.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><strong>1. The analyzer.</strong> <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our investment analyzer</a> takes any Grand Strand address and returns an estimated market rent with the cash flow. It is a screening estimate, not an appraisal. It is the quick answer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><strong>2. An agent.</strong> Ask us. An agent runs the number from current local leases and listings for the house you are looking at, at no cost, before you write the offer. The agent's number is the one to write the offer on.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want to buy a rental?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the address. We run the rent from local leases and listings, with the bedroom count, the location and the condition, before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Have us run the rent</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What comes out of the rent on a Myrtle Beach rental?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rent is the top line. Eight costs come out of it before the loan payment.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Cost</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What it is here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Property tax</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A rental is assessed at 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. The bill is about three times the bill for the same house as a primary residence.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/invest/landlord-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Insurance</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A landlord policy, wind where it is separate, and flood where the zone or the lender requires it.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Association dues</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Monthly or yearly, on most houses in a planned community. Read the budget before you offer.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/invest/property-management/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Management</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A share of the rent if you hire a manager. National companies publish 10 and 15 percent plans.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Maintenance and repairs</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Set money aside every month. A roof, a heating and cooling system and a water heater each have a date.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Vacancy</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The weeks between tenants, with no rent and the utilities in your name.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Lawn, pest and utilities</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Whatever the lease leaves with the owner. Many leases here leave the lawn with the tenant.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Turnover</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Cleaning, paint and small repairs each time a tenant leaves.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What is left after those costs and the loan payment is the cash flow. <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The analyzer</a> estimates each line for any address. Run the numbers before you offer, not after.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have us help find a new rental.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the area and the budget. We run the rent, each cost and the association documents before you write the offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How much do Myrtle Beach rents change?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Slowly, lately. The metro's typical asking rent moved from about $1,695 in September 2025 to about $1,714 in July 2026, about one percent. In Chapter3's files the first buyers in a new community get the best price for the same rent. <a href="/invest/new-construction-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How a new house works as a rental</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Rent prices FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the fair market rent in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For federal fiscal year 2027: $1,155 for a studio, $1,258 for one bedroom, $1,504 for two, $1,823 for three and $1,981 for four. Forty out of 100 standard homes rent at or below it. It includes utilities.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is the fair market rent the average rent?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. It is the rent that 40 out of 100 standard homes rent at or below, so most standard homes rent for more. The metro's typical asking rent was about $1,714 in July 2026.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How do I find out what my house would rent for?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Enter the address in our investment analyzer for a screening estimate, or ask us and an agent runs the rent from local leases and listings at no cost.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do furnished rentals rent for more in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Per month, yes, on leases shorter than a year, such as furnished stays for traveling nurses and seasonal workers. The trade is more turnover and more work between stays.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/fmr2027/FY27_FMRs.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD, fair market rents FY2027</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD, how fair market rents are defined</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow research data, observed rent index</a>. Read September 7, 2026. Educational only. Benchmarks are area figures; the rent for one house comes from local leases.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Get the rent for the house you are looking at.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">One call. We run the rent from local leases and listings before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div></section></main>
