rial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses in Carolina Forest, seen from above. Carolina Forest is in ZIP code 29579, row 5 of the table.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="up-or-down"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Are rents rising">Is rent going up or down in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Up. Asking rents for houses rose about 3 percent in the last year, to the highest point in Zillow's index.</p><figure class="c3-gchart rp-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .8rem">House rent and house value, change since 2015</span><ul class="rp-key" aria-hidden="true"><li><i style="background:#c4783a"></i>House asking rent</li><li><i style="background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,#1c2028 0 6px,transparent 6px 10px)"></i>House value</li></ul><svg class="rp-n" viewBox="0 0 280 218" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of two Zillow indexes for the Myrtle Beach metro, September of each year from 2015 to 2026, as the change since 2015. The asking rent for a house and the middle-tier house value both rose steeply from 2020 to 2022. Over the last four years the rent kept rising, about 8 percent, while the house value stayed about flat."><rect x="189.6" y="8.4" width="76.4" height="177.4" fill="#c4783a" fill-opacity=".09" rx="6"/><text x="227.8" y="175.1" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">last 4 years</text><line x1="56" x2="266" y1="185.8" y2="185.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".3"/><text x="50" y="190.7" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">0</text><line x1="56" x2="266" y1="143.6" y2="143.6" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="50" y="148.5" text-anchor="end