 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a free rental property calculator for Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, the rental analyzer on this page, for a year-round rental. Enter an address and the price, and say whether you pay cash or take a loan. It fills in the rent and the costs, and Chapter3 AI sums up what the numbers mean."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach a good place to buy a rental property?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For cash flow alone, usually not. The middle house for sale in Carolina Forest or Longs keeps about 4 to 5 percent of its price a year before insurance and a loan. Our target is 6 percent. Over five and ten years, prices in the metro rose faster than our 3 percent target, though they dipped over the last three. Our agents keep a list of investors who buy for a modest cash flow plus that rise."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a Myrtle Beach condo a good investment?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if the rent still covers the dues, and on most condos here it does not. The middle 2-bedroom condo's dues take about a quarter to half of HUD's rent, depending on the area. A condo rented by the night has different numbers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the property tax on a rental in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About $1,206 a year for each $100,000 of value outside city limits, and about $1,528 in the City of Myrtle Beach. A rental is taxed on 6 percent of its value, not 4, and pays the school operating tax."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is landlord insurance on a Myrtle Beach rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is priced house by house, so we get you a quote on the exact home before you make an offer. Flood is a separate policy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you run numbers on a property listed with another brokerage?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Any home on the Grand Strand, listed with any brokerage. We use the listing, the county record, nearby rentals and the association's papers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is running the numbers free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. There is no fee and no obligation. You can send one address or several."}}]}</script>
