0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>June to August</strong><span class="t">47% of the income</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Oceanfront condos for sale, Myrtle Beach</strong><span class="t">95% marked nightly</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Myrtle Beach neighborhoods</strong><span class="t">Mostly lease only</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 4, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Run it yourself, and a two-bedroom Airbnb leaves you more than a lease once guests book it about 82 nights a year. Most city neighborhoods allow only a lease.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A short-term rental, such as an Airbnb, leaves you more than a long-term rental, a yearly lease, once guests book it about 82 nights a year. That figure assumes you run it yourself. At a third of the nights, about 124, the owner of a Myrtle Beach two-bedroom keeps about $8,000 a year more.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many listings book fewer nights. Half of two-bedroom listings take in more than the middle one, and half take in less. Its owner keeps about $3,000 less than with a lease.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of 422 condos for sale in oceanfront buildings inside Myrtle Beach city limits, listing agents marked 402 as allowing nightly stays. Most city neighborhoods allow only stays of 90 days or more.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send us one address. We run it both ways before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us run both numbers</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#which-earns-more" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which earns more</a></li><li><a href="#is-it-allowed" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Is it allowed</a></li><li><a href="#break-even" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Nights to break even</a></li><li>