+Rents on leases of a year or more, by bedrooms and in ten ZIP codes from Little River to Murrells Inlet.
 
 The short answer
-Two public numbers describe long-term rents here. The federal fair market rent for Horry County, fiscal year 2027, is $1,258 for one bedroom, $1,504 for two, $1,823 for three and $1,981 for four. Utilities are included. Forty out of 100 standard homes rent at or below it, so most rent for more. The metro's typical asking rent across all home types was about $1,714 in July 2026. One house rents above or below those numbers on bedroom count, location, condition, whether it is furnished, and lease length. Our analyzer estimates the rent for any address, and an agent runs the number from local leases before you offer.
+A house rents for about $1,600 a month on a new lease in Horry County outside the Loris, Aynor and Green Sea area. The tenant also pays about $200 a month for power, water and gas. That is the middle rent for houses leased in the last two years: half rent for more, and half for less.
+An apartment or condo rents for about $1,100 a month with one bedroom and about $1,150 with two, plus about $100 of utilities. Those apartment figures count leases old and new, so a new lease costs more than that.
 
