-## What comes out of the rent on a Myrtle Beach rental?
-The rent is the top line. Eight costs come out of it before the loan payment.
-Cost What it is here
-Property tax A rental is assessed at 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. The bill is about three times the bill for the same house as a primary residence.
-Insurance A landlord policy, wind where it is separate, and flood where the zone or the lender requires it.
-Association dues Monthly or yearly, on most houses in a planned community. Read the budget before you offer.
-Management A share of the rent if you hire a manager. National companies publish 10 and 15 percent plans.
-Maintenance and repairs Set money aside every month. A roof, a heating and cooling system and a water heater each have a date.
-Vacancy The weeks between tenants, with no rent and the utilities in your name.
-Lawn, pest and utilities Whatever the lease leaves with the owner. Many leases here leave the lawn with the tenant.
-Turnover Cleaning, paint and small repairs each time a tenant leaves.
