+HUD's schedule for the Myrtle Beach-North Myrtle Beach-Conway metro area, from October. The figures include the utilities, except the telephone.
+The voucher program uses it to work out what it pays. The rules for landlords who take vouchers are on our Section 8 rentals page. The three-bedroom figure has risen about 55 percent in ten years.
+
+## Can a landlord raise the rent in South Carolina?
+Yes. A new lease can state a higher rent. During a lease, the rent is the amount the lease states.
+No local rent limits South Carolina does not let a city or county limit rents on privately owned homes.
+
+Thirty days' notice Either side can end a month-to-month lease with thirty days' written notice.
+
+No raise to retaliate A landlord may not raise the rent above market value to punish a tenant who complained to a code agency or to the landlord.
+
+Deposits, notices and the rest of the landlord's rules are on our South Carolina landlord rules page.
 
