-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/sell/">Sell</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Home Value</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Selling a home</p><h1 class="detail-h1">What is my home worth in Myrtle Beach?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)"></em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge, 30+ years on the Grand Strand &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 1, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">A licensed broker tells you what your own Horry County home is worth, free, from the sales most like it.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses and other homes that resold in Horry County went for a middle price of about $350,000 in the 12 months to September 2026, and condos for about $215,000. By area, the middle house price ran from about $234,000 in the city of Loris to about $620,000 in the town of Surfside Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For what your own home is worth, an agent picks the sales most like it and sends you the number with those sales.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send your address. An agent calls the sa