-<div id="page-submarkets-index" class="page-section active"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Neighborhoods</span></div><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin:1rem 0 .5rem">Grand Strand Neighborhoods</p><h1 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2.6rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach neighborhoods.</h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Chapter3 Realty &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 1, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Nine Grand Strand neighborhoods and towns compared, from Conway inland to Pawleys Island south: prices, property tax, flood risk, schools, short-term rental rules and who buys in each.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:620px;margin-bottom:2.5rem;line-height:1.7">Every Grand Strand submarket trades differently. Price, inventory, rental demand, and short-term-rental rules all vary by town. Explore the data and investment profile for each Myrtle Beach area submarket. You can also <a href="/map/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">search the 3D map</a>.</p><a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" class="chooser-card" style="display:block;padding:1.5rem 1.75rem;border:1px solid var(--rule);margin-bottom:1rem;text-decoration:none"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.4rem;color:var(--navy)">Carolina Forest</div><div style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.35rem">The biggest master-planned community: new construction, no city tax, long-term rentals.</div></a><a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" class="chooser-card" style="display:block;padding:1.5rem 1.75rem;border:1px solid var(--