5rem">Start here</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.7rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Start from what you are trying to do</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:.4rem">Nine submarkets is a lot to read through. Find the line that matches your plan and start on that page.</p><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want the highest nightly revenue per property</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Murrells Inlet</a> and <a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Surfside Beach</a>. They lead the Strand on average annual revenue and nightly rate, because the south end is mostly whole houses rather than one- and two-bedroom condos.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want the lowest price to get in</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/conway/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Conway</a> and <a href="/submarkets/little-river/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Little River</a>. Both are yearly-rental markets inland or up the coast, with the lowest entry prices on the Strand and tenant demand that does not depend on the summer.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want schools and a family neighborhood</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Carolina Forest</a>. It is the master-planned inland corridor, the HOAs require long leases rather than nightly stays, and tenant demand follows the school attendance zones.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want the easiest property to buy, rent and resell</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Myrtle Beach</a> or <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">North Myrtle Beach</a>. They hold the great majority of the Strand&#39;s listings, so there is always inventory, always comparable sales, and always a buyer when you sell.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want quiet, and I am buying for myself as much as for yield</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Pawleys Island</a>. Higher nightly rates, lower occupancy, an older and higher-end housing stock, and a buyer pool motivated as much by using the place as renting it.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want to be near the water without oceanfront pricing</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Garden City</a>. The peninsula has ocean on one side and the inlet on the other, and creek-side homes with dock access sit well below the oceanfront blocks.</p></div></div></div></section>
 </main>
 <section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Talk to a licensed Grand Strand agent.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.6);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Get straight answers on pricing, neighborhoods, and the financing that fits, from a licensed local agent.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Speak to a Licensed Agent</a></div></div></section><footer>
