-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Is North Myrtle Beach better for families?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It is known for a quieter, family oriented feel than central Myrtle Beach while still offering steady vacation-rental demand."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How is vacation-rental demand in North Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Established and steady, particularly in beach proximate communities like Cherry Grove and Ocean Drive."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you need a permit to short-term rental in North Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No separate permit. The city requires a business license for every short-term rental, renewed each year. The owner also collects and pays the accommodations taxes. There is no rental permit, inspection or local-agent rule."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can an out-of-state owner run an Airbnb in North Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. The city does not require a local agent or a local manager. The owner lists an emergency contact on the business license application."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What are the neighborhoods in North Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The city formed in 1968 from four communities still used as area names: Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach, and Windy Hill, plus resort communities like Barefoot Resort."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What are property taxes on a second home in North Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In North Myrtle Beach that makes a second home's bill about 3 times a primary home's on the same house."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which schools serve North Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Public schools fall within the North Myrtle Beach attendance area of Horry County Schools. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment for an address on the district boundary map."}}]}</script>
