+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is North Myrtle Beach part of Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. North Myrtle Beach is its own city in Horry County, South Carolina. Four beach towns joined to form it in 1968, and it has its own city tax and rental rules. The Myrtle Beach oceanfront is about 30 minutes south by car."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the sections of North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The four old beach towns are Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach and Windy Hill. Tilghman Beach, Little River Neck, the mainland west of US 17 and the neighborhoods across the waterway make eight parts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you drive a golf cart in North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, from sunrise to sunset, on city streets posted 35 mph or less, with a state permit sticker from the DMV and a licensed driver. A cart may cross Ocean Boulevard, 27th Avenue South, US 17 and Sea Mountain Highway, but not drive along them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are dogs allowed on the beach in North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, on a leash. From May 15 to Labor Day they must be off the beach from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. In that season the beach takes umbrellas only, no tents or canopies."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does it cost to own a home in North Myrtle Beach each year?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As your home, before any mortgage, about $8,400 for a typical house and about $11,000 for a typical condo. That covers tax, insurance, a flood policy outside the zone, the condo fee and upkeep."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the property tax in North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On a house the county values at $565,000, about $2,500 a year as your home and about $7,500 as a second home or rental."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is North Myrtle Beach safe?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. We pull the reported crime figures for the area around any house you ask about."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which schools serve North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Horry County Schools assigns schools by address. North Myrtle Beach is one of its nine attendance areas, with North Myrtle Beach High School, North Myrtle Beach Middle School and Ocean Drive Elementary. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like."}}]}</script>
